Article 24
The duties and functions of FPKK as referred to in Article 23 paragraph (2) consist of:
a. coordinating and synchronizing prevention, services, and empowerment for women and children victims of violence;
b. maintaining and developing FPKK in the prevention, services, and empowerment of victims of violence through networking and a referral system;
c. conducting education on non-discrimination values towards women and children;
d. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence;
e. collecting, compiling, and presenting reports of data on victims of violence; and
f. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence.

Article 13
Efforts to prevent violence against children, in addition to being carried out by the regional government apparatus as referred to in Article 12, shall involve:
a. parents and/or family;
b. the community;
c. educational institutions;
d. child social welfare institutions; and/or
e. other institutions engaged in the field of concern for child protection.

Article 3
The protection of women and children victims of violence is implemented based on the principles of:
a. gender responsiveness;
b. non-discrimination;
c. equal and respectful relationships;
d. maintaining privacy and confidentiality;
e. providing a sense of safety and comfort;
f. respecting individual differences;
g. non-judgmental;
h. respecting the choices and decisions of victims;
i. sensitivity to the background and condition of victims;
j. use of language that is appropriate and understood by the victim;
k. fast and simple;
l. empathy; and
m. best interests of the victim.

CHAPTER VII
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 25
(1) The community may participate in the protection of Victims.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out through:
a. provision of safe houses and/or shelters;
b. establishment and management of orphanages for children;
c. establishment of child rehabilitation centers;
d. active supervision of violence against women and children and reporting to the competent authorities;
e. providing first aid to victims;
f. reporting the occurrence of violence against women and children and providing protection;
g. forming family partners at the village level by the community; and
h. other forms of community participation related to the implementation of protection of women and protection of children.

Article 9
(1) Forms of protection services for women victims of violence include: a. legal aid services;
b. health services;
c. social rehabilitation services;
d. repatriation and social reintegration services;
e. complaint, consultation, and counseling services; and/or f. assistance services.
(2) Protection services for women as referred to in paragraph (1) include receiving and sending case referrals from or to other service units in a networked manner.
(3) Implementation of protection services for women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by Regional Apparatus having main duties and functions in the field of women's empowerment.
(4) Further provisions regarding the forms and procedures for protection services for women victims of violence shall be regulated by a Regent Regulation.

